# webshop-robert — Cursor project rules

## Canonical document

All backend architecture, layering, security, testing, and quality rules live in:

**`.aiassistant/rules/BACKEND_RULES.md`**

Treat that file as the **single source of truth**. Read and follow it in full for any backend work. If this file and `BACKEND_RULES.md` disagree, **`BACKEND_RULES.md` wins**.

## Non-exhaustive summary

- **`api`**: HTTP boundary only—controllers (**routing**), DTOs, syntactic validation, DTO ↔ domain mapping at the edge, Spring Security / web filters, global HTTP exception mapping. **No** application or domain **`@Service`** use-case classes.
- **`core`**: Domain model, ports, repository interfaces, **`RbacService`**, and **all** application/domain **`@Service`** orchestration.
- **Tests**: **Integration tests** (DB, Liquibase, JPA adapters, transactions, business flows through **`core` services**) belong in **`core/src/test`** (or a dedicated IT Maven module). **`api/src/test`** is for **HTTP contract** tests only (e.g. MockMvc: routes, status codes, security boundary, JSON)—not the sole home for full business+persistence coverage.

For payment modules, persistence layout, money rules, and everything else, see **`BACKEND_RULES.md`**.
